<title>CROATIA: Croatia February M1 money supply shrinks, M4 rises.</title>
<headline>Croatia February M1 money supply shrinks, M4 rises.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Croatia issued the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> CROATIA MONEY SUPPLY	   FEBRUARY    JANUARY     FEB '96</p>
<p> Reserve money (million HRK)  8,091.3     8,331.3     6,510.6</p>
<p> Money M1			  10,679.0    10,683.0     8,296.6</p>
<p> Broadest money M4	     38,274.7    37,374.4    26,477.2</p>
<p>NOTE -- February reserve money fell 2.88 percent from January.</p>
<p>M1 money supply, including cash outside banks, their demand deposits and deposits at the central bank, shrank 0.04 percent. Broadest money M4, or total liquid assets, rose 2.41 percent on a monthly level.</p>
<p>-- Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
